, principled move that maximizes White’s initiative early on.\n\nReason: Developing knights or bishops is fine, but **P: d2-d4** seizes central space, opens two key diagonals, and accelerates development by freeing the queen and bishop. It is the most ambitious and consistent with opening principles to gain an advantage.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-d4'}
