ason:**  \nDeveloping knights before bishops is often flexible. Placing the knight on c3 supports the d5 push later and keeps all options open. The bishop on c1 can go to g5 or f4 next turn after the knight is out. No pawn weaknesses are created, and the king remains safe.  \n\n**Answer:** N: b1-c3'}
