n b6 (NBF1 at b6, I misread as c6 earlier). Still, e5 challenges the center and can lead to tactics due to the pinned d4 pawn after White’s bishop develops.  \n\nGiven the options, **P: e4-e5** looks best to seize central initiative immediately.\n\n**Answer:** P: e4-e5'}
